WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:07.025
As I was saying, the press, because of
the space it takes up and how big it is,

2
00:00:08.076 --> 00:00:14.650
finds it easy to blow
up an issue that's small.

3
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.178
Its role is to communicate, but sometimes,

4
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:23.902
careless about what's said,
it tends to give the impression

5
00:00:23.986 --> 00:00:29.740
that small issues end
up becoming big ones.

6
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.292
And that sometimes
makes people start to form

7
00:00:34.602 --> 00:00:37.959
an image of a certain area that,
in reality,

8
00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:40.660
isn't what actually exists there.

9
00:00:40.744 --> 00:00:45.216
So that's what I meant
when I said that the press

10
00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:49.450
finds it easy to turn small
problems into big problems.

11
00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:54.920
And when the media come here,
what do you think they come for?

12
00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.123
Well, from what we've been seeing,

13
00:00:59.214 --> 00:01:03.410
when they arrive, the idea is precisely
to come and gather some material.

14
00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:05.697
We, as residents,

15
00:01:05.781 --> 00:01:11.516
always aim to share our lived experiences,
and we think

16
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.791
our experiences could be reported
just as they were captured.

17
00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:20.463
But what has struck us as strange, what
we've been feeling, is this strangeness,

18
00:01:20.694 --> 00:01:26.548
and that strangeness has led
to a certain closing off

19
00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:32.760
when it comes to communication,
or to what we should share:

20
00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:37.575
it's the reports from the press
that we've been watching.

21
00:01:37.886 --> 00:01:39.003
When they go on air,

22
00:01:39.087 --> 00:01:43.726
instead of showing the positive things,
it's always negative situations.

23
00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:47.974
I don't know if the aim is to denigrate
the neighbourhood, or to make it look

24
00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:53.495
like a threat to the people
who live around us.
